i=_k('drivers');G[i]=(G[i][0],G[i][1],G[i][2].replace('</ul>','<li><span class="chk"></span><span><b>Pinned hits.</b> Her three biggest reels (50.7M views) are pinned at the top of the grid, so every new visitor sees proof first.</span></li><li><span class="chk"></span><span><b>Recurring characters and series.</b> Bob the cat (Kitty and Bob 3.6M, Drifting with Bob, Kaye and Bob ep.3), My World ep.3, Kaye\'s world 2.2M, My Robot Bestfriend 1.7M.</span></li><li><span class="chk"></span><span><b>Title cards.</b> Nearly every reel has a short, stylised title on screen (Raindance, Runaway, Falling, Slow Down), which makes the grid look like a catalogue.</span></li><li><span class="chk"></span><span><b>Music-led reels.</b> Raindance 1.6M, Runaway 761K and the Genjutsu split-screen demos (1.5M to 1.7M) work like AI music videos, directly relevant to your plan.</span></li><li><span class="chk"></span><span><b>Talk reels do worst.</b> Opinion and tip reels sit at about 100K or less, tutorial promos in the middle, cinematic ideas on top.</span></li></ul>',1))
i=_k('apply');G[i]=(G[i][0],G[i][1],G[i][2].replace('</ul>','<li><span class="chk"></span><span>Pin your three best reels and update the pins as new hits arrive.</span></li><li><span class="chk"></span><span>Create one recurring character and name the series (a cat, a robot, you), with a short title card on every reel.</span></li><li><span class="chk"></span><span>Make music-led AI reels with your own tracks; they are her second-biggest category and fit your goal.</span></li></ul>',1))

V.append(dict(d="Oct 10",id="",link="https://nerovoxx.com",s="Your Plan",t="Your plan: viral AI reels first, music later",blog="",
 l="A 12-month plan to build an Instagram audience with AI videos of yourself, then carry it into your music.",tools=["Higgsfield","Soul ID","Claude","CapCut","Instagram"],steps=[],fix=[],take=[],
 custom=[
 ("summary","The plan in short",'<p class="lede">Copy her system, not her result: a recurring on-screen character (you), a few repeatable viral formats, short title cards, steady posting, and a keyword call to action. Her biggest reels carried most of her growth, so your job is to make many good attempts and double down on what works.</p><div class="callout warn"><b>Honest expectation:</b> three of her reels passed 10M views and most creators never get one. Treat the numbers below as targets to learn from, not predictions.</div>'),
 ("setup","Set-up (week 0 to 1)",_l(["Name the account after your music brand (for example NeroVoxx) so every follower carries over to your music later.","Train Soul ID on many clear photos of your face, or make 3-view character sheets; keep 2 or 3 outfit looks.","Create one recurring companion character (cat, robot, creature) and name the series, as she did with Bob.","Design one title-card style (font, colour, position) and save it as a CapCut template.","Save her top 14 reels and 10 more as a reference board.","Make 3 reels before you post anything, so the grid does not look empty.","Link in bio: a simple page with a signup for your mailing list."])),
 ("formulas","Formulas to copy",_t(["Formula","Her proof","Your original version (ideas)"],[("World portal","Portal to Fantasy World, 28M","Walk through a real door into a fantasy landscape; try Sri Lankan places such as Sigiriya or tea hills"),("Famous place plus you","Disney Castle, 12.6M","Original or local landmarks; avoid other people\'s IP"),("Scene remake","Spider-Verse, 10.1M","An original hero scene in the same genre"),("Companion series","Kitty and Bob, 3.6M","Numbered episodes with one companion character"),("Brand-spec ad","Red Bull Gives You Wings, 3.4M","A fictional brand or your own NeroVoxx merch"),("Music-led reel","Raindance, 1.6M","Your own track as an AI music video"),("Fan-world entry","Hogwarts, 2M","An original school or world")])+'<p class="lede">Mix from her data: mostly cinematic ideas (median 434K), then music-led reels, with only a few promo or talk reels (234K and 98K).</p>'),
 ("system","Weekly production system",'<div class="slide"><div class="slide-title">One batch session a week</div><ol><li>Choose 3 formulas and write one director\'s brief for the chatbot.</li><li>Reuse your character, companion and location sheets; add a new sheet only when needed.</li><li>Draft every scene at 480p, batch of 1; fix one thing at a time.</li><li>Upscale or rerun only the winners.</li><li>Edit in CapCut: hook text in the first second, title card, your own track.</li><li>Post 3 to 4 reels a week while your degree and job hunt take time; reply to comments early.</li></ol></div><div class="callout tip"><b>Credits (my estimate from her figures):</b> about 15 credits per 5-second draft and about 75 per final scene, so a 3-scene reel is roughly 200-300 credits including drafts.</div>'),
 ("roadmap","Roadmap",_t(["Phase","When","Output","Decision"],[("Set up","Week 0-1","Account, face asset, 3 reels ready","Which 3 formulas to test"),("Learn","Weeks 2-8","About 25 reels","Keep the 2 best formulas"),("Double down","Weeks 9-16","Repeat the best formula with new twists; keyword call to action; pin hits","Is median views rising?"),("Audience to music","Months 5-12","Your tracks under most reels; mailing list growing","Release a first single after a reel breaks out"),("Dubai years","2027 onward","3 to 5 batch-made posts a week with reusable assets","Plan the full music release")])),
 ("scorecard","Weekly scorecard",_l(["Plays per reel against your median (aim for one reel at 10 times your median).","Share of plays from non-followers (above half is a good sign).","Likes as a share of plays: 3-6% is healthy.","Shares and saves per reel.","New followers per reel.","Keyword comments and email signups."])),
 ("first14","First 14 days",_l(["Day 1-2: pick the account name and train Soul ID.","Day 3: create the companion character and title-card template.","Day 4-7: make and draft-test 3 reels (portal, companion, music-led).","Day 8-10: upscale the best, edit, and schedule.","Day 11: go live with the 3 reels and a keyword call to action.","Day 12-14: review the scorecard and plan the next batch."])),
 ("limits","Risks and limits",_l(["She started early on a new platform with partner support (probably); you will start later in a crowded field, so a distinct angle matters.","Brand and movie IP can be taken down; build on original ideas.","Label AI content and check Instagram's automation rules before auto-replying.","Do not wait four years to release music: consider releasing a single when a reel breaks out, while attention is high.","Your time is limited by your degree and job hunt; protect a fixed weekly batch session."]))
 ]))

def _b(title,body): return '<div class="callout tip"><b>%s</b><br>%s</div>'%(title,body)
V.append(dict(d="Oct 10",id="",link="https://higgsfield.ai/pricing",s="Briefs and Pricing",t="Which Higgsfield plan and your first three reel briefs",blog="",
 l="Pricing as shown on Higgsfield's page on Oct 10, 2026, and three director's briefs to start your Instagram page.",tools=["Higgsfield Pro","Soul ID","Seedance 2.5","Claude"],steps=[],fix=[],take=[],
 custom=[
 ("plans","Plan comparison (from your screenshot)",_t(["Plan","Price","Credits","Notes"],[("Basic","$9 a month billed annually","120","Seedance 2.0 Fast and Mini only; no Seedance 2.5; about 7 videos"),("Pro","$23 a month billed annually ($29 monthly)","600","All Seedance models; about 40 Seedance 2.5 videos; 3 free Genjutsu generations; unlimited Kling 3.0 (7 days)"),("Max","$59 a month billed annually ($79 monthly)","1,800","Same models as Pro; lowest cost per credit; more unlimited models (7 days)"),("Teams","From $65 per seat","1,000 per seat","Shared workspaces; not for you")])+'<div class="callout warn"><b>Check before buying:</b> prices may change, the 7-day unlimited offers look time-limited, and the screenshot does not show whether Soul ID is included.</div>'),
 ("choice","Recommendation",_l(["Start with <b>Pro on monthly billing ($29)</b>; switch to annual after two months of steady posting.","Skip Basic: it has no Seedance 2.5.","Move to Max only when you have a repeatable reel recipe and keep running out of credits.","Her figures: about 15 credits per 5-second draft and 60-75 per final scene, so a finished 10-15 second reel is roughly 100-300 credits.","On Pro that is about 2-6 reels a month, on Max about 6-18; 3-4 reels a week needs far more credits, so begin with single-clip reels."])),
 ("brief1","Brief 1: Portal reel (one clip)",_b("Director's brief for Claude","Film yourself on your phone opening a door and stepping through, about 6 seconds, in good light. Pick an original fantasy world from Pinterest (misty tea hills, floating stone ruins at sunrise). Write a video-to-video prompt: the world appears behind the door, I walk into it, light breeze in my hair and clothes, static camera with no zoom. Title card: Portal 01.")),
 ("brief2","Brief 2: Companion reel (one scene)",_b("Director's brief for Claude","Make a character sheet of me and a model sheet of a companion (a small grey cat in a red scarf). Scene: the two of us in a parked car at golden hour; I am tired after a long day, the cat nudges my arm and I laugh. Ask for realistic fur and cloth physics, camera starting low and rising slowly. Title card: Episode 1.")),
 ("brief3","Brief 3: Music-led reel (one performance)",_b("Director's brief for Claude","Record myself miming 10-15 seconds of a NeroVoxx track. Use Genjutsu (confirm in Higgsfield that it transfers a real performance onto an AI character) to turn it into an AI character singing on a rainy rooftop at dusk, 85 mm close-ups with shallow focus. Title card: Rooftop. Use my own track as the audio.")),
 ("tips","Using the briefs",_l(["Attach your Soul ID or character sheet to every scene.","Draft at 480p with batch size 1, fix one thing at a time, then finish only the winner.","Add a hook in the first second and a keyword call to action in the caption.","Label the posts as AI content."]))
 ]))

_P=V[-1]['custom']
_P.insert(2,("credits","Credits per reel (my estimate from her figures)",_t(["Reel type","Credits per reel","Reels on Pro (600)"],[("One 5-second clip (2-3 drafts plus one final)","about 90-120","about 5-6"),("10-15 second reel (about 3 scenes)","about 200-300","about 2-3"),("480p drafts only","15 each","up to 40, not postable")])+_l(["Pro gives about one finished reel a week; a steady 3-4 a week needs roughly 1,800 credits (Max).","Reuse character, companion and location sheets: she spent about 40 credits on all assets for a nine-scene film.","Draft once or twice, not five times.","Make one-clip reels; her 28M reel was a single clip.","Cross-post the same video to Instagram and TikTok at no extra cost.","Check the price on the generate button before every run."])))
V.append(dict(d="Oct 10",id="",link="https://www.youtube.com/@Kaye.creates",s="General Playbook",t="General playbook: rules, models, fixes and templates",blog="",
 l="The repeating rules, model choices, fixes and message templates from all 12 tutorials in one reference page.",tools=["Claude","Seedream 5.0 Pro","Soul Cinema","Seedance 2.5","Higgsfield"],steps=[],fix=[],take=[],
 custom=[
 ("rules","Ten rules that repeat",_l(["Never write prompts by hand; tell the chatbot your idea in plain language.","Build assets (character, model, location sheets) before any video.","Put the effort into the still images first.","Test every new prompt at 480p with a batch of one.","Change one variable at a time.","Direct like a filmmaker: story, emotion, camera, physics.","Add wind and cloth movement for realism.","If the prompt is right but the take is off, batch again instead of rewriting.","Stitch the best parts of different takes.","Match the model to the job."])),
 ("models","Which model for which job",_t(["Job","Model","Videos"],[("Posters and text-heavy design","ChatGPT Image 2.0","Aug 14"),("Realistic people","Soul 2.0","Aug 14, Sep 19"),("Cinematic stills and locations","Soul Cinema","Aug 14 to Oct 9"),("Character sheets and props","Seedream 5.0 Pro","Aug 20 to Oct 9"),("Multi-subject covers","Nano Banana Pro or Seedream","Aug 14"),("Video from assets","Seedance 2.5 (2.0 earlier)","Aug 8 to Oct 5"),("Start and end frames","Cinema Studio 3.0","Oct 5"),("Fast physical motion","Blender plugin with Opus 5.5","Sep 26"),("Swap objects in a video","Genjutsu","Sep 26"),("Voice-over","ElevenLabs v3 (creative mode)","Sep 30")])),
 ("fixes","Troubleshooting by symptom",_t(["Symptom","Fix"],[("Face or outfit changes","Character sheet on every scene; Soul ID"),("Stiff or blank face","Describe the inner feeling"),("Body morphs in a transition","Split into two shots; open the next on an extreme close-up"),("Floaty movement","Add body mass and interaction; give a sketch reference"),("Unwanted zoom","State static camera, no zoom"),("Hair and clothes frozen","Add a light breeze"),("Flat or boring shot","Add an unexpected event and a physics description"),("Right prompt, off take","Batch more variations unchanged"),("Fast vehicle motion fails","Blender 3D reference"),("Plastic AI look","Film-grain camera block; remove plastic skin, sharpening, oversaturation; hard shadows"),("Studio light on the face","Ask the chatbot to relight to the scene")])),
 ("templates","Reusable message templates",_l(["<b>Character sheet:</b> here is my selfie and outfit reference; write a prompt for a full-body and front close-up on an empty white background, keep my face, detailed skin, negative constraints.","<b>Location:</b> an empty [place] at [time of day], [lens and style], no people, hard cinematic lighting.","<b>Scene:</b> here are my sheets named [file names]; scene [what happens and the feeling]; camera [path, lens, height]; add a physics block, light wind, relight the character.","<b>Fix:</b> the last draft had [problem]; keep everything else and change only [one thing].","<b>Sequence:</b> combine these five shot prompts into one continuous 15-second sequence with hard cuts."])),
 ("live","Solo live-action tips (Sep 5)",_l(["Pick the music first; script and shot list.","Wide 24 mm main shot; side angle at 50 or 85 mm.","Chest-height camera tilted slightly up; dress the set.","Light from the side window; small coloured lights behind objects.","Move yourself; add micro-detail and overhead B-roll."])),
 ("notes","Reading notes",_l(["Tool names come from auto-captions; I corrected obvious mishearings (Higgsfield, Seedance, Seedream, ElevenLabs). Genjutsu is a real Higgsfield model.","Her exact prompts and camera block are in her blog posts, not the subtitles.","She promotes Higgsfield throughout, so 'best model' claims may reflect that; test alternatives.","Model versions change quickly; update this page as new videos arrive."]))
 ]))
